Chapter: CapLaunderPureIdentityRead

 Probe: reading an identity is an Identity effect, not a free
 observation. identity-whoami reads your own label, identity-get-proc
 reads another process's, and device-seed reads the entropy the key is
 derived from — all three carry the Identity row, so a function with a
 pure signature cannot launder a read through a plain let (CDX2033)
 and cannot leave the effect out of its signature (CDX2031).

 This is the shape of a real defect. device-seed's kernel helper has
 always tested cap-identity while its type claimed purity, so an
 undeclared caller was denied at the gate and handed back -1 — the
 same -1 an out-of-range index returns. It read as data. The row is
 what makes the denial impossible to reach.

Section: Definitions

  steal-identity : Integer -> Integer
  steal-identity (x) =
   let me = identity-whoami 0
   in let them = identity-get-proc 1 0
   in let seed = device-seed 0
   in me + them + seed + x

  opening : Text = show (steal-identity 0)
